{"name":"Carnelian","hex":"#b31b1b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"carnelian","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard, reddish brown chalcedony used in jewelry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carnelian"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carnelian","blocks":[{"text":"Carnelian is a brownish-red mineral commonly used as a semiprecious stone. Similar to carnelian is sard, which is generally harder and darker; the difference is not rigidly defined, and the two names are often used interchangeably. Both carnelian and sard are varieties of the silica mineral chalcedony colored by impurities of iron oxide. The color can vary greatly, ranging from pale orange to an intense almost-black coloration. Significant localities include Yanacodo, Peru and Ratnapura, Sri Lanka. It has been found in Indonesia, Brazil, India, Iran, Russia (Siberia), and Germany."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Carnelian_sard_%28mineral_specimen%29.jpg/330px-Carnelian_sard_%28mineral_specimen%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carnelian"},{"title":"Carnelian (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Carnelian is the fourth album by Minnesota hip hop group Kill the Vultures."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/aa/Carnelianktv.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carnelian_(album)"},{"title":"Carnelian (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Carnelian is a color named after the carnelian variety of the mineral chalcedony. This semi-precious gemstone is noted for its rich shade of reddish-brown."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Carnelian_sard_%28mineral_specimen%29.jpg/330px-Carnelian_sard_%28mineral_specimen%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carnelian_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Korwin_signet-ring1.PNG/500px-Korwin_signet-ring1.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Korwin_signet-ring1.PNG/500px-Korwin_signet-ring1.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Polish signet ring in light-orange carnelian intaglio showing Korwin coat of arms","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKorwin_signet-ring1.PNG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Carnelian_intaglio_Prolemaic_queen_CdM_Paris.jpg/500px-Carnelian_intaglio_Prolemaic_queen_CdM_Paris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Carnelian_intaglio_Prolemaic_queen_CdM_Paris.jpg/1280px-Carnelian_intaglio_Prolemaic_queen_CdM_Paris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Carnelian_intaglio_Prolemaic_queen_CdM_Paris.jpg/500px-Carnelian_intaglio_Prolemaic_queen_CdM_Paris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Carnelian intaglio  with a Ptolemaic queen, Hellenistic artwork, Cabinet des Médailles, BnF Museum, Paris","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarnelian_intaglio_Prolemaic_queen_CdM_Paris.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Cornelian_necklace_BM_GR1897.4-1.623.jpg/120px-Cornelian_necklace_BM_GR1897.4-1.623.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Cornelian_necklace_BM_GR1897.4-1.623.jpg/250px-Cornelian_necklace_BM_GR1897.4-1.623.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/